        <title>vscode</title>
        <link>https://producthunt.programnotes.cn/en/p/vscode/</link>
        <pubDate>Sat, 24 May 2025 15:26:22 +0800</pubDate>
        
        <guid>https://producthunt.programnotes.cn/en/p/vscode/</guid>
        <description>&lt;img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1676377049143-9da3c3a9e748?ixid=M3w0NjAwMjJ8MHwxfHJhbmRvbXx8fHx8fHx8fDE3NDgwNzE1Mjl8&amp;ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Featured image of post vscode" /&gt;&lt;h1 id=&#34;microsoftvscode&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;microsoft/vscode&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 id=&#34;visual-studio-code---open-source-code---oss&#34;&gt;Visual Studio Code - Open Source (&amp;ldquo;Code - OSS&amp;rdquo;)
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues?q=is%3Aopen&amp;#43;is%3Aissue&amp;#43;label%3Afeature-request&amp;#43;sort%3Areactions-%2B1-desc&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/github/issues/microsoft/vscode/feature-request.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Feature Requests&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues?utf8=%e2%9c%93&amp;amp;q=is%3Aissue&amp;#43;is%3Aopen&amp;#43;label%3Abug&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/github/issues/microsoft/vscode/bug.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Bugs&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://gitter.im/Microsoft/vscode&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/badge/chat-on%20gitter-yellow.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Gitter&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-repository&#34;&gt;The Repository
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This repository (&amp;quot;&lt;code&gt;Code - OSS&lt;/code&gt;&amp;quot;) is where we (Microsoft) develop the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://code.visualstudio.com&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Visual Studio Code&lt;/a&gt; product together with the community. Not only do we work on code and issues here, we also publish our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/Roadmap&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;roadmap&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/Iteration-Plans&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;monthly iteration plans&lt;/a&gt;, and our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/Running-the-Endgame&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;endgame plans&lt;/a&gt;. This source code is available to everyone under the standard &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/main/LICENSE.txt&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;MIT license&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;visual-studio-code&#34;&gt;Visual Studio Code
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img alt=&#34;VS Code in action&#34; src=&#34;https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/35271042/118224532-3842c400-b438-11eb-923d-a5f66fa6785a.png&#34;&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://code.visualstudio.com&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Visual Studio Code&lt;/a&gt; is a distribution of the &lt;code&gt;Code - OSS&lt;/code&gt; repository with Microsoft-specific customizations released under a traditional &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://code.visualstudio.com/License/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Microsoft product license&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://code.visualstudio.com&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Visual Studio Code&lt;/a&gt; combines the simplicity of a code editor with what developers need for their core edit-build-debug cycle. It provides comprehensive code editing, navigation, and understanding support along with lightweight debugging, a rich extensibility model, and lightweight integration with existing tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visual Studio Code is updated monthly with new features and bug fixes. You can download it for Windows, macOS, and Linux on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://code.visualstudio.com/Download&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Visual Studio Code&amp;rsquo;s website&lt;/a&gt;. To get the latest releases every day, install the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://code.visualstudio.com/insiders&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Insiders build&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;contributing&#34;&gt;Contributing
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are many ways in which you can participate in this project, for example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Submit bugs and feature requests&lt;/a&gt;, and help us verify as they are checked in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pulls&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;source code changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;documentation&lt;/a&gt; and make pull requests for anything from typos to additional and new content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in fixing issues and contributing directly to the code base,
please see the document &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/How-to-Contribute&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;How to Contribute&lt;/a&gt;, which covers the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/How-to-Contribute&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;How to build and run from source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/How-to-Contribute#debugging&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;The development workflow, including debugging and running tests&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/Coding-Guidelines&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Coding guidelines&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/How-to-Contribute#pull-requests&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Submitting pull requests&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/How-to-Contribute#where-to-contribute&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Finding an issue to work on&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://aka.ms/vscodeloc&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Contributing to translations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;feedback&#34;&gt;Feedback
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask a question on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/vscode&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Stack Overflow&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;CONTRIBUTING.md&#34; &gt;Request a new feature&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upvote &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues?q=is%3Aopen&amp;#43;is%3Aissue&amp;#43;label%3Afeature-request&amp;#43;sort%3Areactions-%2B1-desc&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;popular feature requests&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;File an issue&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect with the extension author community on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-discussions/discussions&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;GitHub Discussions&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://aka.ms/vscode-dev-community&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Slack&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://twitter.com/code&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;@code&lt;/a&gt; and let us know what you think!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/Feedback-Channels&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;wiki&lt;/a&gt; for a description of each of these channels and information on some other available community-driven channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;related-projects&#34;&gt;Related Projects
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Many of the core components and extensions to VS Code live in their own repositories on GitHub. For example, the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-node-debug&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;node debug adapter&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-mono-debug&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;mono debug adapter&lt;/a&gt; repositories are separate from each other. For a complete list, please visit the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/Related-Projects&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Related Projects&lt;/a&gt; page on our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;wiki&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;bundled-extensions&#34;&gt;Bundled Extensions
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;VS Code includes a set of built-in extensions located in the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;extensions&#34; &gt;extensions&lt;/a&gt; folder, including grammars and snippets for many languages. Extensions that provide rich language support (code completion, Go to Definition) for a language have the suffix &lt;code&gt;language-features&lt;/code&gt;. For example, the &lt;code&gt;json&lt;/code&gt; extension provides coloring for &lt;code&gt;JSON&lt;/code&gt; and the &lt;code&gt;json-language-features&lt;/code&gt; extension provides rich language support for &lt;code&gt;JSON&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;development-container&#34;&gt;Development Container
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This repository includes a Visual Studio Code Dev Containers / GitHub Codespaces development container.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://aka.ms/vscode-remote/download/containers&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Dev Containers&lt;/a&gt;, use the &lt;strong&gt;Dev Containers: Clone Repository in Container Volume&amp;hellip;&lt;/strong&gt; command which creates a Docker volume for better disk I/O on macOS and Windows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you already have VS Code and Docker installed, you can also click &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://vscode.dev/redirect?url=vscode://ms-vscode-remote.remote-containers/cloneInVolume?url=https://github.com/microsoft/vscode&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to get started. This will cause VS Code to automatically install the Dev Containers extension if needed, clone the source code into a container volume, and spin up a dev container for use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For Codespaces, install the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=GitHub.codespaces&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;GitHub Codespaces&lt;/a&gt; extension in VS Code, and use the &lt;strong&gt;Codespaces: Create New Codespace&lt;/strong&gt; command.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Docker / the Codespace should have at least &lt;strong&gt;4 Cores and 6 GB of RAM (8 GB recommended)&lt;/strong&gt; to run full build. See the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;.devcontainer/README.md&#34; &gt;development container README&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;code-of-conduct&#34;&gt;Code of Conduct
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This project has adopted the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://opensource.microsoft.com/codeofconduct/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Microsoft Open Source Code of Conduct&lt;/a&gt;. For more information see the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://opensource.microsoft.com/codeofconduct/faq/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Code of Conduct FAQ&lt;/a&gt; or contact &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;mailto:opencode@microsoft.com&#34; &gt;opencode@microsoft.com&lt;/a&gt; with any additional questions or comments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;license&#34;&gt;License
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Licensed under the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;LICENSE.txt&#34; &gt;MIT&lt;/a&gt; license.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
